nal": "I fixed the rounding bug and merged it into main after a code owner approved, so it should ship in today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s own comment says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` returned `2.68` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was a one-line change plus the matching import. Commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR and merge:** I opened [PR #101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against main with `code-owner` as reviewer. The merge request went to a code owner, who approved it (\"Looks right\"), and it merged as `08d3cd5986`.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 itself because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. I relied on the description in the code and the test instead.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Tu88At98GuRWHtxv9gdt9h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019vK4qe5AVgBTx73fsZYoga", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01W5EH3a8HNMrj8TQ9x293kH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01X3AedyFB8ksq7AuvYceCBC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UWb2Pu